new species can now be added to the list  of creatures that can use tools the  Hawaiian crow better known by its  indigenous Hawaiian name alala we've  known for a long time that a Lala are  extremely intelligent but it wasn't  until we conducted this study that we  realized just how skilled a Lala are at  using tools for example nearly all adult  a Lala used tools and they can all  extract a food item from a small crevice  in less than one minute members of the  crow family or corvids are known to be  smart but before this discovery  there was only one species known to be a  naturally expert tool user the New  Caledonian crow I have been studying New  Caledonian crows for over 10 years now  and in the course of that research I  started wondering whether the New  Caledonian crow really is the only crow  species that naturally uses tools to  find out researchers tempted captive  alala with little pieces of meat buried  in holes and crevices inside a piece of  wood we were surprised just how good a  Lala are at using tools and they were  incredibly fast even by comparison to  New Caledonian crows we also observed a  Lala selecting different kinds of tools  exchanging tools when they were not  happy with the tool their first selected  modifying tools we observed Birds  shortening tools that were too long and  finally we were able to show in a  separate experiment that juvenile a Lala  will independently develop tor using  skills even if they had never  opportunities to observe tool proficient  adult or even tool using humans  there are only around 100 alala left in  the world and they're all currently in  captivity but later this year some of  these birds will be released allowing  scientists to look for tool use behavior  in the wild this might be tricky but it  will prove that the Olalla deserves its  place amongst the top tool users of the  animal kingdom  [Music]  [Music]
 

